From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Berkay=20K=C3=B6sebay?= <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 21:36:01 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: apple: Add S8000 MCA driver
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

CPU DAI for the A9 MCA ("mca-version 4"), following iOS 16.7.10's
AppleAE2MCA::_setIISConfig_v4: reset and flush with bounded polls,
sample size, FIFO watermarks, slot masks, TX/RX configuration and the
frame register. Start enables the direction and sets the frame run bit;
stop resets the direction. Playback and capture share the frame: the
first prepared direction programs the whole block, the second one only
its own half, and the frame stops with the last one.

Samples move through SmartIO DMA (MCA0: endpoints 0x28 and 0x29) with
the generic dmaengine PCM. The SmartIO shim record of the endpoint goes
to the DMA driver as the slave config's peripheral_config: the transfer
width from the ADT dma-channels entry (0x21 16-bit, 0x22 32-bit), the
shim timeout, FIFO and trigger words, and one millisecond of samples as
the FIFO depth, as AppleAE2MCA sets it up. The PCM is limited to 16
periods (one firmware command each) and marked BATCH, since the position
advances per period.

The MCA's MCLK control word is exported as a clock (iOS writes 0x58,
nclk/2 with the output enabled, for the codec's 12 MHz MCLK). While a
stream is prepared, the driver routes the MCA to its pad in the shared
i2s-switch, with the codec as the clock provider.

Interrupts: only the FIFO error causes are unmasked, per prepared
direction, and an error cause is masked again after it fires, since it
re-latches every frame while the condition lasts. The IRQ is enabled
only while the block is powered.

Speakers and the stereo DMIC capture work on J71t (iPad 5) under
PipeWire.

Signed-off-by: Berkay Kösebay <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
[Orchard: from brkosebay/linux 5fb5d260, eef262be, fccffe15 and the
 squash 3e47c1c2 (J71t ledger 10.5), omarchy-ipad5 patches/audio
 0004/0012/0015-0017 and capture-jack. Reviewed to mainline practice:
 dropped the timer and PIO PCMs with the nodma, mclk_ctl and route
 parameters, the debugfs files and the bring-up counters and timings;
 SoC constants (MCLK word and rate, SmartIO shim words) in match data;
 the i2s-switch route is computed from the switch node and pad index
 with the encoding from iOS's route compiler instead of raw register
 pairs from DT (same values for MCA0 on pin 0).]
Co-developed-by: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Signed-off-by: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 sound/soc/apple/Kconfig     |  15 +
 sound/soc/apple/Makefile    |   2 +
 sound/soc/apple/s8000-mca.c | 872 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 889 insertions(+)
